    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="1123" n="973" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6200/–1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Schuyler to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d344-f1"/> herewith a copy of a part of the Monitorul Oficial for
                    to-day, which contains the original text in French and a translation into
                    Roumanian of the treaty of commerce and navigation between Roumania and France,
                    concluded at Paris on March 6, 1907, and approved by the Roumanian Senate on
                    March 9 (22), to which is appended a “Declaration” and an “Arrangement”
                    concerning the protection of works of literature and art which places France and
                    Roumania reciprocally on the footing of the most favored nations.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montgomery
                    Schuyler.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
